a big night for the clark county school  district after months and months of  contention superintendent dr jesus  jarrah returning to his seat during  tonight's regular board meeting the  board fired him in october then  rescinded that decision just last month  sasha loftis joins us with more on the  agreement made between jarrah and the  board sasha  brian and kirsten some may call this the  culmination of months of turmoil all  eyes will be on dr jarrah tonight as he  attends his first ccsd board meeting in  person since he was originally  terminated by the board back in october  we obtained this agreement between dr  jesus jarrah and the ccsd board of  trustees citing better cooperation  moving forward it did shed some light on  past conflicts saying the board will  communicate about meeting agendas only  use authority as a group not a single  trustee acting alone and discuss dr  jarrah's claims of harassment the  agreement was signed by dr jarrah board  president linda cavazos irene cepeda and  evelyn garcia morales trustee daniel  ford later released this statement  saying she was quote excluded from board  attorney meetings for purportedly  violating confidentiality  we did reach out to trustee ford  regarding that and she did confirm that  she was excluded from the meeting where  the board and its attorney discussed  this agreement now in terms of the  agreement it does also state that if any  board members do not stick with this  plan they will be disciplined now of  course stay with 8 news now for the  latest as we continue to follow this  meeting tonight reporting live sasha  loftis live local now
 

